answer:
When filing for the registration of a new biological product, the applicant must submit a single process containing the following documents, in addition to the petition forms and proof of payment:

*   Declaration of the company's size (economic capacity) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the Company's Operating License and/or Sanitary Permit [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the Company's Authorization Certificate or its publication in the Official Gazette (DOU) [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the updated Technical Responsibility Certificate issued by the Regional Pharmacy Council [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Technical justification for the product registration [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the Good Manufacturing Practices Certificate (CBPF) issued by Anvisa for all manufacturers of the active ingredient, bulk biological product, primary packaging, finished biological product, diluent, and adjuvant [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the CBPF issued by the competent sanitary authority of the country where the manufacturer of the active ingredient, bulk biological product, primary packaging, finished biological product, diluent, and adjuvant is located [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   History of the product's registration status in other countries, if applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the registration proof in the country of origin, issued by the respective competent Sanitary Authority [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the package insert model approved by the competent sanitary authority of the country of origin, with a sworn translation [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Models of the package insert and primary and secondary packaging, in accordance with current legislation [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Updated pharmacovigilance data, in accordance with current sanitary legislation, obtained from clinical studies and product marketing, when applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Barcode (GTIN) for all presentations or identification and security mechanisms that allow product tracking [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Copy of the national, international, or internal company compendium with the specifications of the finished biological product [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Additional information on TSE (Transmissible Spongiform Encephalopathy) control, when applicable [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Technical report [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Therapeutic experimentation report [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Pharmacovigilance report [RDC 55/2010, Art. 30];
*   Clinical study protocols and reports, including pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics, and pivotal safety and efficacy studies [RDC 55/2010, Art. 46].

Additionally, the technical report must contain detailed information regarding the manufacturer, product data (composition, indications, storage, etc.), development history, manufacturing stages, quality control, storage and transport validation, excipients, stability studies, contaminants, and packaging specifications [RDC 55/2010, Art. 31]. For biotechnological products, specific information regarding cell banks and characterization of the active substance must also be provided [RDC 55/2010, Art. 34].

